罢工持续了太久，导致那些剧集没能复播。

256
00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:54.730
So we were actually really fortunate.
所以我们其实真的很幸运。

257
00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:55.450
Yeah.
是啊。

258
00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:57.030
Well, there you go, guys.
好吧，情况就是这样，伙计们。

259
00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:58.550
Lady, that's all I got.
女士，我就知道这些了。

260
00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:00.690
I have a fun little thing.
我有个有趣的小东西。

261
00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:02.390
It's not a fast fact.
这不是什么快问快答。

262
00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.230
Maybe it's a Kinsey tidbit.
也许算是个金赛小花絮吧。

263
00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:05.230
What is it?
是什么？

264
00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:10.410
Jenna, do you remember that Ed would do an impression of Tom Brokaw?
珍娜，你还记得艾德会模仿汤姆·布罗考吗？

265
00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:11.450
Yes.
记得。

266
00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:13.150
And it would make us laugh.
那总能把我们逗笑。

267
00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:14.190
It was so good.
模仿得太像了。

268
00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.070
It would make us laugh so hard.
总能把我们笑得前仰后合。

269
00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:16.870
Okay.
好的。

270
00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:22.470
So what he would do is, Ed, as Tom Brokaw, he would start out telling a news story, and
他当时是这么做的，艾德会模仿汤姆·布罗考，先开始播报一则新闻，然后

271
00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:25.950
then he would tell us what our hot snack of the day was on set.
告诉我们当天片场的特色零食是什么。

272
00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:32.270
And there was a particular time where we had albondigas soup, and he made that into part
有一次我们正好喝了墨西哥肉丸汤，他把这个也编进了

273
00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:37.310
of Tom Brokaw's news announcement, and on the DVD commentary, they were talking about
汤姆·布罗考的新闻播报里，在DVD评论音轨里，他们还聊到了

274
00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:38.710
it, and Ed did it.
这件事，然后艾德就现场表演了一段。

275
00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:39.310
Oh!
噢！

276
00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:42.570
Sam, will you play it?
山姆，你能放一下吗？

277
00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:46.970
Could you give us the Tom Brokaw and say the magic word that makes Steve giggle?
你能模仿一下汤姆·布罗考，说出那个让史蒂夫咯咯笑的魔力词吗？

278
00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:54.550
The Israelis have once again launched an all-round assault on albondigas soup.
以色列人再次对墨西哥肉丸汤发起了全面突击。

279
00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.690
That's what keeps us going.
那可是我们的动力源泉。

280
00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:00.290
Nothing better.
没有比这更好的了。

281
00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:00.670
Yes.
是的。

282
00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:00.950
Yep.
没错。

283
00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.480
Gosh, what a gem.
天哪，真是个宝贝。

284
00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:07.260
I'm so happy that has been recorded.
我真高兴那段被录下来了。

285
00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:08.240
I know.
我知道。

286
00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:08.760
I know.
我知道。

287
00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:13.600
So if you guys want to know what behind-the-scenes moments were like, Ed was doing Tom Brokaw,
所以如果你们想知道幕后花絮是什么样的，就是艾德在模仿汤姆·布罗考，

288
00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:17.920
and John was doing impressions, and we were all watching them and just cracking up.
约翰在模仿其他人，我们都在旁边看着，笑得不行。

289
00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:18.900
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

290
00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:23.740
Angela, that actually brought tears of joy to my eyes.
安吉拉，那真的让我热泪盈眶。

291
00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:28.200
I know I'm very tired today, and maybe that's made me a little emotional.
我知道我今天很累，也许这让我变得有点感性了。

292
00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:30.760
But, oh, my goodness.
但是，天哪。

293
00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.320
Wow, that took me back.
哇，那让我回到了过去。

294
00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:33.660
It did me, too, Jenna.
我也是，珍娜。

295
00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:35.640
It just made me laugh, and it warmed my heart.
它让我开怀大笑，也温暖了我的心。

296
00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:37.820
These were the behind-the-scenes moments that I treasure.
这些就是我珍视的幕后时刻。

297
00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:39.060
Oh, all right.
噢，好吧。

298
00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.700
I'm going to let that take me into break.
我要带着这份心情进入休息时间了。

299
00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:41.900
I'm going to pull myself together.
我得平复一下情绪。

300
00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:43.040
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

301
00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.020
All right, guys.
好了，各位。

302
00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:57.960
We are back, and Michael is in a series of very important meetings.
我们回来了，迈克尔正在开一系列非常重要的会议。

303
00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:01.020
The first meeting is with the accounting department.
第一场会议是和会计部门开的。

304
00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:02.620
Seems very serious.
看起来非常严肃。

305
00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:05.320
Pam comes in, hands Michael a Post-it note.
帕姆走进来，递给迈克尔一张便签。

306
00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:08.760
Yes, and Michael says with great authority after reading the note,
是的，迈克尔读完便签后，用非常权威的口吻说道，

307
00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:09.280
you know what?
你知道吗？

308
00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.500
I need to just call them back.
我得给他们回个电话。

309
00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:11.680
I can't talk right now.
我现在没法谈。

310
00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:14.600
Everyone is very perplexed when he does this, by the way.
顺便说一下，他这么做的时候，每个人都感到非常困惑。

311
