00:43:24.480 --> 00:43:28.480
Here is the journal entry that Jan's lawyer reads.
这是简的律师朗读的那篇日记。

932
00:43:28.920 --> 00:43:32.640
I quote from an entry dated January 4 of this past year.
我引用去年1月4日的一篇日记。

933
00:43:49.860 --> 00:44:00.000
But he says eerie.
但他读成了“eerie”（怪异的）。

934
00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:01.620
And then Michael corrects him.
然后迈克尔纠正了他。

935
00:44:02.840 --> 00:44:04.680
Oh, more tomorrow.
噢，明天再说。

936
00:44:05.260 --> 00:44:06.440
XOXO Michael.
么么哒，迈克尔。

937
00:44:07.400 --> 00:44:07.840
Incredible.
难以置信。

938
00:44:08.220 --> 00:44:10.920
Angela, I looked up the definition of eerie.
安吉拉，我查了“eerie”的定义。

939
00:44:11.340 --> 00:44:12.060
You did?
你查了？

940
00:44:12.500 --> 00:44:12.960
Yeah.
是的。

941
00:44:13.200 --> 00:44:15.600
The lawyer thinks he meant eerie.
律师以为他想说的是“怪异的”。

942
00:44:15.880 --> 00:44:17.900
But Michael's like, it's eerie.
但迈克尔的意思是“eerie”（牙买加俚语，意为美好）。

943
00:44:18.100 --> 00:44:19.200
He's been in Jamaica.
他去过牙买加。

944
00:44:19.640 --> 00:44:20.220
Yes.
是的。

945
00:44:20.500 --> 00:44:23.900
And it means nice, good, or pleasing.
它的意思是美好、不错或令人愉悦。

946
00:44:23.900 --> 00:44:28.020
And it is used as a general term of approval in Jamaican English.
在牙买加英语中，它被用作表示赞同的通用词。

947
00:44:28.560 --> 00:44:31.980
So despite everything, he's feeling pretty eerie.
所以尽管发生了这一切，他感觉还是挺“eerie”的。

948
00:44:32.440 --> 00:44:39.280
I have to say, Michael is absolutely crushed and feels betrayed by this reading of his journal.
我不得不说，迈克尔被这次日记朗读彻底击垮了，感到被背叛了。

949
00:44:39.500 --> 00:44:40.180
It is embarrassing.
这确实很尴尬。

950
00:44:40.180 --> 00:44:42.060
And he is right to feel that way.
他有这种感觉是理所应当的。

951
00:44:42.260 --> 00:44:43.100
Jan is horrible.
简太可怕了。

952
00:44:43.420 --> 00:44:44.440
This was horrible.
这太可怕了。

953
00:44:44.460 --> 00:44:46.140
And this was premeditated.
而且这是蓄谋已久的。

954
00:44:46.440 --> 00:44:46.820
Yeah.
没错。

955
00:44:47.060 --> 00:44:48.740
She brought it from their home.
她是从他们家里带来的。

956
00:44:48.740 --> 00:44:51.920
Now they decide, we're going to make copies of the journal.
现在他们决定，我们要把日记复印一下。

957
00:44:52.160 --> 00:44:53.540
We're going to make 10 copies.
我们要复印10份。

958
00:44:53.740 --> 00:44:55.200
Toby's like, actually make it 11.
托比说，干脆印11份吧。

959
00:44:55.700 --> 00:45:00.660
Michael is just sinking further and further into this embarrassing spiral.
迈克尔正一步步陷入这种尴尬的漩涡中。

960
00:45:00.920 --> 00:45:05.380
And Lester talked on the DVD commentary about one of the challenges of writing this episode
莱斯特在DVD评论音轨里谈到，编写这一集面临的挑战之一

961
00:45:05.380 --> 00:45:09.020
was taking Michael through these layers, right?
就是让迈克尔经历这些层层打击，对吧？

962
00:45:09.280 --> 00:45:12.240
At the beginning of the deposition, he's feeling confident.
在取证开始时，他感觉信心满满。

963
00:45:12.440 --> 00:45:15.640
And slowly with each layer, it's just all falling apart.
但随着每一层的剥离，一切都在慢慢崩溃。

964
00:45:15.640 --> 00:45:19.220
It's hard to believe that it's going to get worse from here.
很难相信接下来情况还会变得更糟。

965
00:45:19.340 --> 00:45:20.360
And yet it does.
然而事实确实如此。

966
00:45:20.540 --> 00:45:21.520
It's so tragic.
真是太悲剧了。

967
00:45:21.880 --> 00:45:29.040
And now they go to lunch and everyone in this corporate lunchroom is reading his journal.
现在他们去吃午饭，公司食堂里的每个人都在读他的日记。

968
00:45:29.400 --> 00:45:33.040
All I could think of was corporate has a cafeteria.
我当时满脑子想的都是，公司居然有食堂。

969
00:45:35.200 --> 00:45:38.740
I believed it, Jenna, because you know those big buildings in New York.
我信了，珍娜，因为你知道纽约那些大楼。

970
00:45:38.960 --> 00:45:39.580
I do.
我知道。

971
00:45:39.920 --> 00:45:42.060
They have cafeterias and food areas.
它们都有食堂和用餐区。

972
00:45:42.620 --> 00:45:45.420
Lady, I love a corporate cafeteria.
天哪，我超爱公司食堂。

973
00:45:45.640 --> 00:45:47.000
I'll tell you what.
我跟你说。

974
00:45:47.140 --> 00:45:52.520
I only experienced it once when I worked at the Coca-Cola bottling company in Los Angeles.
我在洛杉矶的可口可乐装瓶厂工作时，只体验过一次。

975
00:45:52.680 --> 00:45:54.580
It's where they bottle the soda.
那是他们装瓶汽水的地方。

976
00:45:54.840 --> 00:45:57.320
I worked on the complaint hotline there.
我在那儿的投诉热线工作。

977
00:45:57.500 --> 00:45:58.240
You did?
真的吗？

978
00:45:58.560 --> 00:45:59.500
I did.
真的。

979
00:45:59.500 --> 00:46:02.280
I took all of the complaints.
我负责接听所有的投诉。

980
00:46:02.740 --> 00:46:08.480
And basically the policy was anyone who called to complain got free coupons for soda.
基本上政策就是，任何打电话来投诉的人都能得到免费的汽水优惠券。

981
00:46:08.720 --> 00:46:13.420
I had to listen to all the complaints and log all the complaints and then mail the coupons.
我得听完所有的投诉，记录所有的投诉，然后把优惠券寄出去。

982
00:46:13.580 --> 00:46:14.420
That was my job.
那就是我的工作。

983
00:46:14.420 --> 00:46:16.160
So it's kind of off in a remote area.
所以它有点偏僻。

984
00:46:16.160 --> 00:46:19.180
This factory, you get 30 minutes for lunch.
在这个工厂，午餐时间只有30分钟。

985
00:46:19.400 --> 00:46:20.280
There's nowhere to go.
没地方可去。

986
00:46:20.280 --> 00:46:24.560
So you had to bring your lunch or they had a corporate cafeteria.
所以你得自带午餐，或者去公司食堂。

987
00:46:24.560 --> 00:46:28.680
And lady, all the soda was free.
而且天哪，所有的汽水都是免费的。

988
00:46:29.040 --> 00:46:29.280
Hey!
嘿！

989
00:46:29.900 --> 00:46:32.440
You could drink as much as you wanted all day.
你可以整天想喝多少就喝多少。

990
00:46:32.780 --> 00:46:35.540
The fountain sodas were free.
喷泉汽水是免费的。

991
00:46:35.820 --> 00:46:37.980
But I love a cafeteria.
但我就是喜欢食堂。

992
00:46:37.980 --> 00:46:39.540
I don't know what it is about it.
我不知道为什么，但我就是喜欢。

993
00:46:39.540 --> 00:46:41.100
I liked it when I was in high school.
我上高中的时候就喜欢。

994
00:46:41.160 --> 00:46:42.620
I loved it in college.
上大学时我也超爱。

995
00:46:43.080 --> 00:46:44.420
I love a cafeteria.
我就是喜欢食堂。

996
00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:47.400
This is going to melt your brain for a moment.
接下来这件事可能会让你瞬间大脑宕机。

997
00:46:47.880 --> 00:46:54.280
About a year and a half ago, I met my friend, Derek Haas, who works on Chicago Fire, Chicago
大约一年半前，我遇到了我的朋友德里克·哈斯，他在《芝加哥烈焰》和《芝加哥警署》工作。

998
00:46:54.280 --> 00:46:54.600
PD.
PD。

999
00:46:54.940 --> 00:46:56.040
He's like the showrunner creator.
他是剧集运作人兼创作者。

1000
00:46:56.220 --> 00:46:58.060
He's like amazing, talented writer.
他是一位了不起的、才华横溢的编剧。

1001
00:46:58.300 --> 00:46:59.360
We went to college together.
我们大学时就在一起了。

1002
00:46:59.560 --> 00:47:01.520
He's like, Ange, come have lunch.
他说，安吉，来吃个午饭吧。

1003
00:47:01.600 --> 00:47:02.200
Let's catch up.
我们叙叙旧。

1004
00:47:02.300 --> 00:47:03.200
I'm like, awesome.
我说，太棒了。

1005
00:47:03.580 --> 00:47:06.660
He's like, you know, our office is on Universal Studio Lot.
他说，你知道吗，我们的办公室就在环球影城片场。

1006
00:47:06.660 --> 00:47:07.460
I said, yeah.
我说，好啊。

1007
00:47:07.700 --> 00:47:08.960
He was like, so come meet me.
他说，那来找我吧。

1008
00:47:09.000 --> 00:47:12.860
We'll go to the NBC Universal Commissary.
我们去NBC环球的员工餐厅。

1009
00:47:13.080 --> 00:47:14.000
I said, what?
我说，什么？

1010
00:47:14.300 --> 00:47:15.420
He said, have you never been?
他说，你从来没去过吗？

1011
00:47:15.780 --> 00:47:17.260
You're on an NBC show.
你可是NBC节目的演员啊。

1012
00:47:17.740 --> 00:47:22.800
I was like, no, we filmed over in this little soundstage in the middle of nowhere.
我说，没去过，我们是在一个荒郊野外的摄影棚拍的。

1013
00:47:23.160 --> 00:47:26.320
He said, oh yeah, NBC has an amazing commissary.
他说，哦对，NBC的员工餐厅棒极了。

1014
00:47:27.060 --> 00:47:27.540
What?
什么？

1015
00:47:28.480 --> 00:47:31.040
Jenna, it looks like you're at the Four Seasons.
珍娜，那感觉就像在四季酒店一样。

1016
00:47:31.260 --> 00:47:33.680
I'm talking like fabric napkin.
我是说，那种布餐巾。

1017
00:47:33.920 --> 00:47:36.380
The water glasses that are the big glasses.
还有那种大号的水杯。

1018
00:47:36.380 --> 00:47:39.900
You know, where your iced tea comes with like a lemon wedge.
你知道的，就是那种冰茶里会放一片柠檬的餐厅。

1019
00:47:40.540 --> 00:47:40.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1020
00:47:41.200 --> 00:47:45.440
Jenna, we never got the NBC Commissary treatment, but it was really good.
珍娜，我们虽然没享受过NBC餐厅的待遇，但那里的东西确实很好吃。

1021
00:47:45.860 --> 00:47:51.240
I also went there years, years later to have lunch with Terry Weinberg, who is one of the
后来过了好多年，我又去那儿和泰瑞·温伯格吃过午饭，她是

1022
00:47:51.240 --> 00:47:53.260
executive producers of the office.
《办公室》的执行制片人之一。

1023
00:47:53.620 --> 00:47:55.120
She works on the lot.
她在片场工作。

1024
00:47:55.460 --> 00:47:58.820
She invited me for lunch at the commissary, and I thought the same thing.
她邀请我去餐厅吃午饭，当时我也产生了同样的想法。

1025
00:47:59.220 --> 00:48:06.100
I thought, wow, Greg could have chosen to have our show on the lot, but he wanted
我想，哇，格雷格本可以选在片场拍我们的剧，但他想

1026
00:48:06.100 --> 00:48:11.560
us to be more independent and have our own space, which ultimately I loved and was the
让我们更独立，拥有自己的空间，最终我非常喜欢这个决定，这也是

1027
00:48:11.560 --> 00:48:12.260
right decision.
正确的决定。

1028
00:48:13.160 --> 00:48:14.900
Except for that damn cafeteria.
除了那个该死的食堂。

1029
00:48:15.360 --> 00:48:17.120
I mean, I would have really liked that.
我是说，我其实挺想去那儿的。

1030
00:48:17.320 --> 00:48:18.880
That cafeteria was legit.
那个食堂真的很正宗。

1031
00:48:19.300 --> 00:48:23.500
This is not to say that we didn't have the greatest food on our set because our caterers
这并不是说我们片场的伙食不好，因为我们的餐饮服务商

1032
00:48:23.500 --> 00:48:24.160
were amazing.
非常棒。

1033
00:48:24.160 --> 00:48:26.700
I just really like a cafeteria experience.
我只是真的很喜欢食堂的那种体验。

1034
00:48:26.700 --> 00:48:28.660
It's not the food, necessarily.
不一定是因为食物。

1035
00:48:28.660 --> 00:48:33.400
I love the tray, and you go down the little thing with the silver bars.
我喜欢那种托盘，还有沿着银色栏杆排队取餐的感觉。

1036
00:48:33.560 --> 00:48:35.100
You know, I love a soup plantation.
你知道的，我超爱自助餐厅。

1037
00:48:35.400 --> 00:48:36.540
This is why, I think.
我想这就是原因吧。

1038
00:48:37.120 --> 00:48:39.300
Lady, you don't have to even talk about this with me.
大姐，你根本不用跟我说这些。

1039
00:48:39.340 --> 00:48:41.600
You've heard my thoughts on a Vegas buffet.
你又不是不知道我对拉斯维加斯自助餐的看法。

1040
00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:42.500
I know.
我知道。

1041
00:48:43.020 --> 00:48:44.640
It's just things we like.
这只是我们喜欢的东西而已。

1042
00:48:45.140 --> 00:48:49.180
Guess where we filmed these corporate cafeteria scenes, Angela?
安吉拉，你猜我们是在哪儿拍的这些公司食堂的戏份？

1043
00:48:49.640 --> 00:48:51.340
I know, but I'm not going to say.
我知道，但我不想说。

1044
00:48:51.540 --> 00:48:52.200
You tell us.
你告诉我们吧。

1045
00:48:52.660 --> 00:48:56.080
At the Universal Studios Commissary.
就在环球影城的员工餐厅。

1046
00:48:56.680 --> 00:48:57.660
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

1047
00:48:57.940 --> 00:48:59.780
We filmed them for one day.
我们拍了一天。

1048
00:48:59.940 --> 00:49:03.560
We rented the entire space so everyone who was working there didn't get to eat lunch
我们包下了整个场地，所以那天在那儿工作的人都没法吃午饭了，

1049
00:49:03.560 --> 00:49:07.980
there that day because all the people in the background were hired by us for non-speaking
因为背景里所有的人都是我们雇来的，

1050
00:49:07.980 --> 00:49:08.440
roles.
演的是无台词角色。

1051
00:49:08.600 --> 00:49:13.620
We had that cafeteria that day to shoot these lunch scenes.
那天我们包下了食堂来拍摄这些午餐场景。

1052
00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:17.860
Well, Jenna, Michael is walking around the cafeteria, and he doesn't know where to sit.
嗯，珍娜，迈克尔在食堂里走来走去，他不知道该坐在哪里。

1053
00:49:17.860 --> 00:49:19.300
But everyone's reading his journal.
但每个人都在读他的日记。

1054
00:49:19.660 --> 00:49:21.260
He's feeling a bit loSt.
他感到有点迷茫。

1055
00:49:21.420 --> 00:49:26.180
And you know he's at the bottom of the barrel when he goes and sits with Toby.
你知道当他去和托比坐在一起时，他已经跌入谷底了。

1056
00:49:26.640 --> 00:49:28.220
And Toby tries.
而托比还试图努力。

1057
00:49:28.720 --> 00:49:30.520
Toby is so kind.
托比真是太善良了。

1058
00:49:31.100 --> 00:49:31.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1059
00:49:31.620 --> 00:49:35.520
He brings up his parents' divorce and how it made him feel.
他提到了他父母的离婚，以及这件事让他有什么感受。

1060
00:49:35.760 --> 00:49:37.680
Both of his parents wanted him to testify.
他的父母都想让他出庭作证。

1061
00:49:37.680 --> 00:49:40.120
And he's like, but I just love them both so much.
他说，但我真的很爱他们俩。

1062
00:49:40.660 --> 00:49:41.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1063
00:49:41.080 --> 00:49:46.520
And he's sort of saying, Michael, I know you love Jan and you love Dunder Mifflin.
他其实是在说，迈克尔，我知道你爱简，也爱邓德·米夫林公司。

1064
00:49:46.640 --> 00:49:49.520
So I see how you're pulled in two directions, too.
所以我明白你为什么也感到左右为难了。

1065
00:49:49.640 --> 00:49:50.700
That's the subtext.
这就是潜台词。

1066
00:49:51.260 --> 00:49:54.340
Michael responds by pushing Toby's tray onto the floor.
迈克尔的回应是把托比的餐盘推到了地上。

1067
00:49:54.500 --> 00:49:56.360
And his entire lunch goes with it.
他的整份午餐也随之掉落。

1068
00:49:56.680 --> 00:49:58.620
So Lester talked about this moment.
莱斯特谈到了这个瞬间。

1069
00:49:58.820 --> 00:50:04.620
He said in the script they had written where Michael just goes off on Toby, like makes a
他说剧本里写的是迈克尔对托比大发雷霆，比如发表了一段

1070
00:50:04.620 --> 00:50:05.360
big speech.
长篇大论。

1071
00:50:05.360 --> 00:50:06.820
And they filmed it that way.
他们也确实那样拍了。

1072
00:50:07.000 --> 00:50:10.980
And then Paul Lieberstein pitched, hey, why don't we do one take where he just shoves
然后保罗·利伯斯坦提议说，嘿，我们为什么不拍一条，让他直接把

1073
00:50:10.980 --> 00:50:14.440
my tray off the table and walks away and doesn't even respond to me.
我的餐盘从桌上推掉，然后走开，甚至都不回应我呢？

1074
00:50:14.680 --> 00:50:15.600
And they did it.
他们照做了。

1075
00:50:15.760 --> 00:50:18.280
It was just like in the moment, idea in the moment.
这完全是即兴的，当下的灵感。

1076
00:50:18.480 --> 00:50:19.680
And that's what made it in.
最后成片用的就是这一版。

1077
00:50:19.900 --> 00:50:20.680
So good.
太棒了。

1078
00:50:20.980 --> 00:50:21.860
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1079
00:50:22.180 --> 00:50:28.440
When the deposition continues, they are still reading Michael's diary.
当取证继续进行时，他们还在读迈克尔的日记。

1080
00:50:28.840 --> 00:50:29.780
They have some questions.
他们有一些问题。

1081
00:50:29.940 --> 00:50:33.780
They say, who is this other woman, Ryan, who you refer to?
他们问，你提到的这个叫瑞安的“另一个女人”是谁？

1082
00:50:34.280 --> 00:50:35.240
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1083
00:50:36.420 --> 00:50:38.380
Toby cannot keep his composure.
托比无法保持镇定。

1084
00:50:38.840 --> 00:50:40.540
He is cracking up.
他笑得前仰后合。

1085
00:50:42.140 --> 00:50:50.740
Michael just so looks up to Ryan and his admiration of Ryan is one of my favorite little tidbits
迈克尔非常崇拜瑞安，他对瑞安的这种仰慕是我在剧中

1086
00:50:50.740 --> 00:50:51.440
of the show.
